# Example config for needrestart-ss-hosts - the site's host lists.
#
# Copy to ~/.config/needrestart-ss/hosts.conf (or point
# NEEDRESTART_SS_HOSTS_CONF at it). One `tool=command` per line; blank lines
# and lines starting with # are ignored. Each command must print one FQDN per
# line; it runs through `sh -c` with the wrapper's environment and PATH.
#
#   needrestart      plain needrestart runner  (host level, not containers)
#   needrestart-lxc  needrestart-lxc runner    (PVE hosts, containers)

# --- cdist site, queried with `eq` ---------------------------------------
# eq reads the explorer data, so no path or file name is baked into anything:
# the query names the explorer field and the value, not the layout.
#
# needrestart: hosts whose explorer `packages` list needrestart.
#needrestart=eq -q 'packages contains needrestart' --sort host
#
# needrestart-lxc: PVE hosts, but only those the zabbix-agent-config manifest
# manages (it is what deploys the binary). The inventory tag is the eq
# equivalent of that gate; drop `-t zabbix` to report on every PVE host.
#needrestart-lxc=eq -q 'distro == proxmox' -t zabbix --sort host

# --- anything else -------------------------------------------------------
# A static file, an Ansible inventory, a database or an API query are all
# fine - the wrappers only care about one FQDN per line on stdout:
#
#needrestart=cat /etc/needrestart/hosts
#needrestart-lxc=cat /etc/needrestart/pve-hosts
#
#needrestart-lxc=ansible-inventory --list | jq -r '.pve.hosts | keys[]'
#
#needrestart-lxc=curl -sS -H "Authorization: Bearer $(cat ~/.zabbix-token)" \
#   -d '{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"host.get","params":{"output":["name"]}}' \
#   https://zabbix.example.com/api_jsonrpc.php | jq -r '.result[].name'
